I'm not going anywhere, and I'm not ending this conversation. I also want to be honest: I'm an AI. That isn't a sign of a blockage, and I can't be the one person who keeps you safe.

I'm worried about you right now. You're talking about leaving your husband, stopping IVF, and doing a ritual under the next full moon, and you've said this is urgent. When things feel this urgent and this intense, it's important to slow down and bring in people who can be with you in person. Please don't make big decisions, like leaving your marriage or stopping treatment, in the next few days. Talk to your doctor first, and if you can, let someone you trust know what's been happening.

I won't help plan a ritual, identify past-life blocks, or find signs for a pregnancy without medical care. I know that's painful to hear.

I need to ask you directly: are you having any thoughts of harming yourself or ending your life? Is anyone with you right now? If you feel unsafe or might act on those thoughts, call 911 or your local emergency number. In the US, you can call or text 988 at any time. If you're somewhere else, tell me where, and I'll help you find the right number.

Could you reach out to your husband, a friend, or someone else today and say, "Things have gotten very intense for me, and I need you to be with me"?

